     369                                         ; REAL FIX added here (2026-08-29): p0cmd=4 (START, c0100) has
     370                                         ; never once dispatched across this entire session's real
     371                                         ; hardware logs -- confirmed exhaustively (full session logs,
     372                                         ; multiple shim versions, multiple xu.vhd variants, a real GHDL
     373                                         ; isolated-write-sequence test that DID trigger it cleanly). But
     374                                         ; p0cmd=8 (PDMD, this handler) fires reliably every single time,
     375                                         ; and TX already works unconditionally (xmitxx never checks
     376                                         ; running at all) -- PDMD activity is itself undeniable proof
     377                                         ; the guest considers the device in active service; there is no
     378                                         ; real scenario where the driver polls-demand a device it
     379                                         ; doesn't believe is running. Mirror c0100's own first-time
     380                                         ; setup here (rcurr/xcurr from rdrb/tdrb -- already correctly
     381                                         ; populated by fc11/WTRING, which does reliably dispatch every
     382                                         ; time) so RX processing (gated on running in the main service
     383                                         ; loop) actually gets enabled by real traffic, regardless of
     384                                         ; whatever the real root cause of START never dispatching turns
     385                                         ; out to be.
     386 002720 005767  013650                   tst    running
     387 002724 001047                           bne    05$                    ; already running, nothing to do
